f":"https:\/\/reviews.gog.com\/v1\/products\/1453298883\/reviews\/6abbac02-96f8-11ea-ab87-fa163e93294d\/votes"},"report":{"href":"https:\/\/reviews.gog.com\/v1\/products\/1453298883\/reviews\/6abbac02-96f8-11ea-ab87-fa163e93294d\/reports"}}},{"id":"2aa0b1dc-9471-11ea-b307-fa163e93294d","productId":"1453298883","rating":{"value":4},"content":{"title":"Enormous potential","description":"It's fun, not for the faint of heart - definitely the most complex zombie apocalypse survival game out there.\nWhile I do appreciate the iron man mode in many games, I never like it when it's non optional; playing for months on a character only to have it get scratched and turn zombie because of a teeny tiny mistake is not fun, it just makes the game very tense and stressful.\nSome might say that it's intended, but again: make it an option and everybody's happy.\nThe truth of the matter is probably that the game remembers a lot of what you visit and savegames end up consisting of thousands of files, so keeping multiple saves is not easy, saving takes a long time - some optimization there (as simple as keeping assets as a fifo list with a count limit instead of time based in an area ?), and even limiting to one manual save \/ playthrough would go a long way, as it stands I'm backing up my saves manually which seems unnecessary.\nThat and the combat being a bit too clunky for my taste is why I'm not going 5 stars on this - but definitely worth keeping an eye on at the very least.\n\nA side note on a review from another user: the game is updated on a regular basis, do keep in mind that you'll need to use Galaxy to install the experimental versions.","language":"en-US"},"reviewer":{"id":"46987533035878901","username":"DanElendil","avatar":{"links":{"gog_image_id":"e380dd5e8249f4ce94a3f215ccf0d99c50bf82e19aacc8e4bc3bd02da7c7e8c6","small":"https:\/\/images.gog.com\/e380dd5e8249f4ce94a3f215ccf0d99c50bf82e19aacc8e4bc3bd02da7c7e8c6_avs.jpg","small_2x":"https:\/\/images.gog.com\/e380dd5e8249f4ce